{"route":"/docs/4.4/components/popovers/","version":"4.4","renderedVersion":"4.4","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Popovers","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Documentation and examples for adding Bootstrap popovers, like those found in iOS, to any element on your site."},"blocks":[{"id":"overview","type":"heading","en":"Overview","level":2},{"id":"overview--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Things to know when using the popover plugin:"},{"id":"overview--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"overview--item-1","type":"item","en":"Popovers rely on the 3rd party library <a href=\"https://github.com/floating-ui/popper-docs/blob/main/docs/v1/index.md\">Popper.js</a> for positioning. You must include <a href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/popper.js@1.16.0/dist/umd/popper.min.js\">popper.min.js</a> before bootstrap.js or use <code>bootstrap.bundle.min.js</code> / <code>bootstrap.bundle.js</code> which contains Popper.js in order for popovers to work!"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"overview--item-2","type":"item","en":"Popovers require the <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/components/tooltips/\">tooltip plugin</a> as a dependency."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"overview--item-3","type":"item","en":"If you’re building our JavaScript from source, it <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/javascript/#util\">requires <code>util.js</code></a>."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"overview--item-4","type":"item","en":"Popovers are opt-in for performance reasons, so <strong>you must initialize them yourself</strong>."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"overview--item-5","type":"item","en":"Zero-length <code>title</code> and <code>content</code> values will never show a popover."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"overview--item-6","type":"item","en":"Specify <code>container: &#39;body&#39;</code> to avoid rendering problems in more complex components (like our input groups, button groups, etc)."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"overview--item-7","type":"item","en":"Triggering popovers on hidden elements will not work."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"overview--item-8","type":"item","en":"Popovers for <code>.disabled</code> or <code>disabled</code> elements must be triggered on a wrapper element."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"overview--item-9","type":"item","en":"When triggered from anchors that wrap across multiple lines, popovers will be centered between the anchors’ overall width. Use <code>.text-nowrap</code> on your <code>&lt;a&gt;</code>s to avoid this behavior."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"overview--item-10","type":"item","en":"Popovers must be hidden before their corresponding elements have been removed from the DOM."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"overview--item-11","type":"item","en":"Popovers can be triggered thanks to an element inside a shadow DOM."}]}]},{"id":"overview--note-1","type":"note","tone":"info","body":[{"id":"overview--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"The animation effect of this component is dependent on the <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> media query. See the <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/accessibility/#reduced-motion\">reduced motion section of our accessibility documentation</a>."}]},{"id":"overview--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Keep reading to see how popovers work with some examples."},{"id":"example-enable-popovers-everywhere","type":"heading","en":"Example: Enable popovers everywhere","level":2},{"id":"example-enable-popovers-everywhere--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"One way to initialize all popovers on a page would be to select them by their <code>data-toggle</code> attribute:"},{"id":"example-enable-popovers-everywhere--code-1","type":"code","value":"$(function () {\n  $('[data-toggle=\"popover\"]').popover()\n})","language":"js"},{"id":"example-using-the-container-option","type":"heading","en":"Example: Using the <code>container</code> option","level":2},{"id":"example-using-the-container-option--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"When you have some styles on a parent element that interfere with a popover, you’ll want to specify a custom <code>container</code> so that the popover’s HTML appears within that element instead."},{"id":"example-using-the-container-option--code-1","type":"code","value":"$(function () {\n  $('.example-popover').popover({\n    container: 'body'\n  })\n})","language":"js"},{"id":"example","type":"heading","en":"Example","level":2},{"id":"example--example-1","type":"demo","key":"cdeb26f11f287ba99929","height":147},{"id":"example--code-1","type":"code","value":"<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-lg btn-danger\" data-toggle=\"popover\" title=\"Popover title\" data-content=\"And here's some amazing content. It's very engaging. Right?\">Click to toggle popover</button>","language":"html"},{"id":"four-directions","type":"heading","en":"Four directions","level":3},{"id":"four-directions--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Four options are available: top, right, bottom, and left aligned."},{"id":"four-directions--example-1","type":"demo","key":"cbad7dbd97a6c20ffb33","height":147},{"id":"four-directions--code-1","type":"code","value":"<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-secondary\" data-container=\"body\" data-toggle=\"popover\" data-placement=\"top\" data-content=\"Vivamus sagittis lacus vel augue laoreet rutrum faucibus.\">\n  Popover on top\n</button>\n\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-secondary\" data-container=\"body\" data-toggle=\"popover\" data-placement=\"right\" data-content=\"Vivamus sagittis lacus vel augue laoreet rutrum faucibus.\">\n  Popover on right\n</button>\n\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-secondary\" data-container=\"body\" data-toggle=\"popover\" data-placement=\"bottom\" data-content=\"Vivamus\nsagittis lacus vel augue laoreet rutrum faucibus.\">\n  Popover on bottom\n</button>\n\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-secondary\" data-container=\"body\" data-toggle=\"popover\" data-placement=\"left\" data-content=\"Vivamus sagittis lacus vel augue laoreet rutrum faucibus.\">\n  Popover on left\n</button>","language":"html"},{"id":"dismiss-on-next-click","type":"heading","en":"Dismiss on next click","level":3},{"id":"dismiss-on-next-click--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Use the <code>focus</code> trigger to dismiss popovers on the user’s next click of a different element than the toggle element."},{"id":"dismiss-on-next-click--note-1","type":"note","tone":"danger","body":[{"id":"specific-markup-required-for-dismiss-on-next-click","type":"heading","en":"Specific markup required for dismiss-on-next-click","level":4},{"id":"specific-markup-required-for-dismiss-on-next-click--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"For proper cross-browser and cross-platform behavior, you must use the <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> tag, <em>not</em> the <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> tag, and you also must include a <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Global_attributes/tabindex\"><code>tabindex</code></a> attribute."}]},{"id":"specific-markup-required-for-dismiss-on-next-click--example-1","type":"demo","key":"3d1c60ee54b7fc348ac6","height":147},{"id":"specific-markup-required-for-dismiss-on-next-click--code-1","type":"code","value":"<a tabindex=\"0\" class=\"btn btn-lg btn-danger\" role=\"button\" data-toggle=\"popover\" data-trigger=\"focus\" title=\"Dismissible popover\" data-content=\"And here's some amazing content. It's very engaging. Right?\">Dismissible popover</a>","language":"html"},{"id":"specific-markup-required-for-dismiss-on-next-click--code-2","type":"code","value":"$('.popover-dismiss').popover({\n  trigger: 'focus'\n})","language":"js"},{"id":"disabled-elements","type":"heading","en":"Disabled elements","level":3},{"id":"disabled-elements--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Elements with the <code>disabled</code> attribute aren’t interactive, meaning users cannot hover or click them to trigger a popover (or tooltip). As a workaround, you’ll want to trigger the popover from a wrapper <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;span&gt;</code> and override the <code>pointer-events</code> on the disabled element."},{"id":"disabled-elements--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"For disabled popover triggers, you may also prefer <code>data-trigger=&quot;hover&quot;</code> so that the popover appears as immediate visual feedback to your users as they may not expect to <em>click</em> on a disabled element."},{"id":"disabled-elements--example-1","type":"demo","key":"6e3b031e6db2c2025073","height":147},{"id":"disabled-elements--code-1","type":"code","value":"<span class=\"d-inline-block\" data-toggle=\"popover\" data-content=\"Disabled popover\">\n  <button class=\"btn btn-primary\" style=\"pointer-events: none;\" type=\"button\" disabled>Disabled button</button>\n</span>","language":"html"},{"id":"usage","type":"heading","en":"Usage","level":2},{"id":"usage--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Enable popovers via JavaScript:"},{"id":"usage--code-1","type":"code","value":"$('#example').popover(options)","language":"js"},{"id":"usage--note-1","type":"note","tone":"warning","body":[{"id":"making-popovers-work-for-keyboard-and-assistive-technology-users","type":"heading","en":"Making popovers work for keyboard and assistive technology users","level":3},{"id":"making-popovers-work-for-keyboard-and-assistive-technology-users--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"To allow keyboard users to activate your popovers, you should only add them to HTML elements that are traditionally keyboard-focusable and interactive (such as links or form controls). Although arbitrary HTML elements (such as <code>&lt;span&gt;</code>s) can be made focusable by adding the <code>tabindex=&quot;0&quot;</code> attribute, this will add potentially annoying and confusing tab stops on non-interactive elements for keyboard users, and most assistive technologies currently do not announce the popover’s content in this situation. Additionally, do not rely solely on <code>hover</code> as the trigger for your popovers, as this will make them impossible to trigger for keyboard users."},{"id":"making-popovers-work-for-keyboard-and-assistive-technology-users--note-text-2","type":"note-text","en":"While you can insert rich, structured HTML in popovers with the <code>html</code> option, we strongly recommend that you avoid adding an excessive amount of content. The way popovers currently work is that, once displayed, their content is tied to the trigger element with the <code>aria-describedby</code> attribute. As a result, the entirety of the popover’s content will be announced to assistive technology users as one long, uninterrupted stream."},{"id":"making-popovers-work-for-keyboard-and-assistive-technology-users--note-text-3","type":"note-text","en":"Additionally, while it is possible to also include interactive controls (such as form elements or links) in your popover (by adding these elements to the <code>whiteList</code> or allowed attributes and tags), be aware that currently the popover does not manage keyboard focus order. When a keyboard user opens a popover, focus remains on the triggering element, and as the popover usually does not immediately follow the trigger in the document’s structure, there is no guarantee that moving forward/pressing <kbd>TAB</kbd> will move a keyboard user into the popover itself. In short, simply adding interactive controls to a popover is likely to make these controls unreachable/unusable for keyboard users and users of assistive technologies, or at the very least make for an illogical overall focus order. In these cases, consider using a modal dialog instead."}]},{"id":"options","type":"heading","en":"Options","level":3},{"id":"options--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Options can be passed via data attributes or JavaScript. For data attributes, append the option name to <code>data-</code>, as in <code>data-animation=&quot;&quot;</code>."},{"id":"options--note-1","type":"note","tone":"warning","body":[{"id":"options--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"Note that for security reasons the <code>sanitize</code>, <code>sanitizeFn</code> and <code>whiteList</code> options cannot be supplied using data attributes."}]},{"id":"options--table-1","type":"table","caption":[],"rows":[{"head":true,"cells":[{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Name"}]},{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Type"}]},{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"Default"}]},{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"Description"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-6","type":"paragraph","en":"animation"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-7","type":"paragraph","en":"boolean"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-8","type":"paragraph","en":"true"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-9","type":"paragraph","en":"Apply a CSS fade transition to the popover"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-10","type":"paragraph","en":"container"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-11","type":"paragraph","en":"string | element | false"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-12","type":"paragraph","en":"false"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-13","type":"paragraph","en":"Appends the popover to a specific element. Example: <code>container: &#39;body&#39;</code>. This option is particularly useful in that it allows you to position the popover in the flow of the document near the triggering element - which will prevent the popover from floating away from the triggering element during a window resize."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-14","type":"paragraph","en":"content"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-15","type":"paragraph","en":"string | element | function"}]},{"type":"td","body":[]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-16","type":"paragraph","en":"Default content value if <code>data-content</code> attribute isn&#39;t present."},{"id":"options--paragraph-17","type":"paragraph","en":"If a function is given, it will be called with its <code>this</code> reference set to the element that the popover is attached to."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-18","type":"paragraph","en":"delay"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-19","type":"paragraph","en":"number | object"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-20","type":"paragraph","en":"0"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-21","type":"paragraph","en":"Delay showing and hiding the popover (ms) - does not apply to manual trigger type"},{"id":"options--paragraph-22","type":"paragraph","en":"If a number is supplied, delay is applied to both hide/show"},{"id":"options--paragraph-23","type":"paragraph","en":"Object structure is: <code>delay: { &quot;show&quot;: 500, &quot;hide&quot;: 100 }</code>"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-24","type":"paragraph","en":"html"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-25","type":"paragraph","en":"boolean"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-26","type":"paragraph","en":"false"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-27","type":"paragraph","en":"Insert HTML into the popover. If false, jQuery&#39;s <code>text</code> method will be used to insert content into the DOM. Use text if you&#39;re worried about XSS attacks."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-28","type":"paragraph","en":"placement"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-29","type":"paragraph","en":"string | function"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-30","type":"paragraph","en":"&#39;right&#39;"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-31","type":"paragraph","en":"How to position the popover - auto | top | bottom | left | right.<br>When <code>auto</code> is specified, it will dynamically reorient the popover."},{"id":"options--paragraph-32","type":"paragraph","en":"When a function is used to determine the placement, it is called with the popover DOM node as its first argument and the triggering element DOM node as its second. The <code>this</code> context is set to the popover instance."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-33","type":"paragraph","en":"selector"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-34","type":"paragraph","en":"string | false"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-35","type":"paragraph","en":"false"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-36","type":"paragraph","en":"If a selector is provided, popover objects will be delegated to the specified targets. In practice, this is used to enable dynamic HTML content to have popovers added. See <a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/issues/4215\">this</a> and <a href=\"https://codepen.io/Johann-S/pen/djJYPb\">an informative example</a>."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-37","type":"paragraph","en":"template"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-38","type":"paragraph","en":"string"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-39","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>&#39;&lt;div class=&quot;popover&quot; role=&quot;tooltip&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;arrow&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;popover-header&quot;&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;popover-body&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#39;</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-40","type":"paragraph","en":"Base HTML to use when creating the popover."},{"id":"options--paragraph-41","type":"paragraph","en":"The popover&#39;s <code>title</code> will be injected into the <code>.popover-header</code>."},{"id":"options--paragraph-42","type":"paragraph","en":"The popover&#39;s <code>content</code> will be injected into the <code>.popover-body</code>."},{"id":"options--paragraph-43","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>.arrow</code> will become the popover&#39;s arrow."},{"id":"options--paragraph-44","type":"paragraph","en":"The outermost wrapper element should have the <code>.popover</code> class."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-45","type":"paragraph","en":"title"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-46","type":"paragraph","en":"string | element | function"}]},{"type":"td","body":[]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-47","type":"paragraph","en":"Default title value if <code>title</code> attribute isn&#39;t present."},{"id":"options--paragraph-48","type":"paragraph","en":"If a function is given, it will be called with its <code>this</code> reference set to the element that the popover is attached to."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-49","type":"paragraph","en":"trigger"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-50","type":"paragraph","en":"string"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-51","type":"paragraph","en":"&#39;click&#39;"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-52","type":"paragraph","en":"How popover is triggered - click | hover | focus | manual. You may pass multiple triggers; separate them with a space. <code>manual</code> cannot be combined with any other trigger."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-53","type":"paragraph","en":"offset"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-54","type":"paragraph","en":"number | string"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-55","type":"paragraph","en":"0"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-56","type":"paragraph","en":"Offset of the popover relative to its target. For more information refer to Popper.js&#39;s <a href=\"https://github.com/floating-ui/popper-docs/blob/main/docs/v1/index.md#modifiers..offset.offset\">offset docs</a>."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-57","type":"paragraph","en":"fallbackPlacement"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-58","type":"paragraph","en":"string | array"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-59","type":"paragraph","en":"&#39;flip&#39;"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-60","type":"paragraph","en":"Allow to specify which position Popper will use on fallback. For more information refer to\n      Popper.js&#39;s <a href=\"https://github.com/floating-ui/popper-docs/blob/main/docs/v1/index.md#modifiers..flip.behavior\">behavior docs</a>"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-61","type":"paragraph","en":"boundary"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-62","type":"paragraph","en":"string | element"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-63","type":"paragraph","en":"&#39;scrollParent&#39;"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-64","type":"paragraph","en":"Overflow constraint boundary of the popover. Accepts the values of <code>&#39;viewport&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;window&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;scrollParent&#39;</code>, or an HTMLElement reference (JavaScript only). For more information refer to Popper.js&#39;s <a href=\"https://github.com/floating-ui/popper-docs/blob/main/docs/v1/index.md#modifiers..preventOverflow.boundariesElement\">preventOverflow docs</a>."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-65","type":"paragraph","en":"sanitize"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-66","type":"paragraph","en":"boolean"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-67","type":"paragraph","en":"true"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-68","type":"paragraph","en":"Enable or disable the sanitization. If activated <code>&#39;template&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;content&#39;</code> and <code>&#39;title&#39;</code> options will be sanitized."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-69","type":"paragraph","en":"whiteList"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-70","type":"paragraph","en":"object"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-71","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/javascript/#sanitizer\">Default value</a>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-72","type":"paragraph","en":"Object which contains allowed attributes and tags"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-73","type":"paragraph","en":"sanitizeFn"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-74","type":"paragraph","en":"null | function"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-75","type":"paragraph","en":"null"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-76","type":"paragraph","en":"Here you can supply your own sanitize function. This can be useful if you prefer to use a dedicated library to perform sanitization."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-77","type":"paragraph","en":"popperConfig"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-78","type":"paragraph","en":"null | object"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-79","type":"paragraph","en":"null"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-80","type":"paragraph","en":"To change Bootstrap&#39;s default Popper.js config, see <a href=\"https://github.com/floating-ui/popper-docs/blob/main/docs/v1/index.md#Popper.Defaults\">Popper.js&#39;s configuration</a>"}]}]}]},{"id":"options--note-2","type":"note","tone":"info","body":[{"id":"data-attributes-for-individual-popovers","type":"heading","en":"Data attributes for individual popovers","level":4},{"id":"data-attributes-for-individual-popovers--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"Options for individual popovers can alternatively be specified through the use of data attributes, as explained above."}]},{"id":"methods","type":"heading","en":"Methods","level":3},{"id":"methods--note-1","type":"note","tone":"danger","body":[{"id":"asynchronous-methods-and-transitions","type":"heading","en":"Asynchronous methods and transitions","level":4},{"id":"asynchronous-methods-and-transitions--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"All API methods are <strong>asynchronous</strong> and start a <strong>transition</strong>. They return to the caller as soon as the transition is started but <strong>before it ends</strong>. In addition, a method call on a <strong>transitioning component will be ignored</strong>."},{"id":"asynchronous-methods-and-transitions--note-text-2","type":"note-text","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/javascript/\">See our JavaScript documentation for more information</a>."}]},{"id":"popoveroptions","type":"heading","en":"<code>$().popover(options)</code>","level":4},{"id":"popoveroptions--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Initializes popovers for an element collection."},{"id":"popovershow","type":"heading","en":"<code>.popover(&#39;show&#39;)</code>","level":4},{"id":"popovershow--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Reveals an element’s popover. <strong>Returns to the caller before the popover has actually been shown</strong> (i.e. before the <code>shown.bs.popover</code> event occurs). This is considered a “manual” triggering of the popover. Popovers whose title and content are both zero-length are never displayed."},{"id":"popovershow--code-1","type":"code","value":"$('#element').popover('show')","language":"js"},{"id":"popoverhide","type":"heading","en":"<code>.popover(&#39;hide&#39;)</code>","level":4},{"id":"popoverhide--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Hides an element’s popover. <strong>Returns to the caller before the popover has actually been hidden</strong> (i.e. before the <code>hidden.bs.popover</code> event occurs). This is considered a “manual” triggering of the popover."},{"id":"popoverhide--code-1","type":"code","value":"$('#element').popover('hide')","language":"js"},{"id":"popovertoggle","type":"heading","en":"<code>.popover(&#39;toggle&#39;)</code>","level":4},{"id":"popovertoggle--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Toggles an element’s popover. <strong>Returns to the caller before the popover has actually been shown or hidden</strong> (i.e. before the <code>shown.bs.popover</code> or <code>hidden.bs.popover</code> event occurs). This is considered a “manual” triggering of the popover."},{"id":"popovertoggle--code-1","type":"code","value":"$('#element').popover('toggle')","language":"js"},{"id":"popoverdispose","type":"heading","en":"<code>.popover(&#39;dispose&#39;)</code>","level":4},{"id":"popoverdispose--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Hides and destroys an element’s popover. Popovers that use delegation (which are created using <a href=\"#options\">the <code>selector</code> option</a>) cannot be individually destroyed on descendant trigger elements."},{"id":"popoverdispose--code-1","type":"code","value":"$('#element').popover('dispose')","language":"js"},{"id":"popoverenable","type":"heading","en":"<code>.popover(&#39;enable&#39;)</code>","level":4},{"id":"popoverenable--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Gives an element’s popover the ability to be shown. <strong>Popovers are enabled by default.</strong>"},{"id":"popoverenable--code-1","type":"code","value":"$('#element').popover('enable')","language":"js"},{"id":"popoverdisable","type":"heading","en":"<code>.popover(&#39;disable&#39;)</code>","level":4},{"id":"popoverdisable--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Removes the ability for an element’s popover to be shown. The popover will only be able to be shown if it is re-enabled."},{"id":"popoverdisable--code-1","type":"code","value":"$('#element').popover('disable')","language":"js"},{"id":"popovertoggleenabled","type":"heading","en":"<code>.popover(&#39;toggleEnabled&#39;)</code>","level":4},{"id":"popovertoggleenabled--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Toggles the ability for an element’s popover to be shown or hidden."},{"id":"popovertoggleenabled--code-1","type":"code","value":"$('#element').popover('toggleEnabled')","language":"js"},{"id":"popoverupdate","type":"heading","en":"<code>.popover(&#39;update&#39;)</code>","level":4},{"id":"popoverupdate--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Updates the position of an element’s popover."},{"id":"popoverupdate--code-1","type":"code","value":"$('#element').popover('update')","language":"js"},{"id":"events","type":"heading","en":"Events","level":3},{"id":"events--table-1","type":"table","caption":[],"rows":[{"head":true,"cells":[{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Event Type"}]},{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Description"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"show.bs.popover"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"This event fires immediately when the <code>show</code> instance method is called."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"shown.bs.popover"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-6","type":"paragraph","en":"This event is fired when the popover has been made visible to the user (will wait for CSS transitions to complete)."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-7","type":"paragraph","en":"hide.bs.popover"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-8","type":"paragraph","en":"This event is fired immediately when the <code>hide</code> instance method has been called."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-9","type":"paragraph","en":"hidden.bs.popover"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-10","type":"paragraph","en":"This event is fired when the popover has finished being hidden from the user (will wait for CSS transitions to complete)."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-11","type":"paragraph","en":"inserted.bs.popover"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-12","type":"paragraph","en":"This event is fired after the <code>show.bs.popover</code> event when the popover template has been added to the DOM."}]}]}]},{"id":"events--code-1","type":"code","value":"$('#myPopover').on('hidden.bs.popover', function () {\n  // do something...\n})","language":"js"}],"demos":[{"key":"cdeb26f11f287ba99929","html":"\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-lg btn-danger\" data-toggle=\"popover\" title=\"Popover title\" data-content=\"And here's some amazing content. It's very engaging. Right?\">Click to toggle popover</button>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"cbad7dbd97a6c20ffb33","html":"\n  <div class=\"bd-example-popovers\">\n    <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-secondary\" data-container=\"body\" data-toggle=\"popover\" data-placement=\"top\" data-content=\"Vivamus sagittis lacus vel augue laoreet rutrum faucibus.\">\n      Popover on top\n    </button>\n    <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-secondary\" data-container=\"body\" data-toggle=\"popover\" data-placement=\"right\" data-content=\"Vivamus sagittis lacus vel augue laoreet rutrum faucibus.\">\n      Popover on right\n    </button>\n    <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-secondary\" data-container=\"body\" data-toggle=\"popover\" data-placement=\"bottom\" data-content=\"Vivamus sagittis lacus vel augue laoreet rutrum faucibus.\">\n      Popover on bottom\n    </button>\n    <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-secondary\" data-container=\"body\" data-toggle=\"popover\" data-placement=\"left\" data-content=\"Vivamus sagittis lacus vel augue laoreet rutrum faucibus.\">\n      Popover on left\n    </button>\n  </div>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example popover-demo"},"sprite":""},{"key":"3d1c60ee54b7fc348ac6","html":"\n<a tabindex=\"0\" class=\"btn btn-lg btn-danger\" role=\"button\" data-toggle=\"popover\" data-trigger=\"focus\" title=\"Dismissible popover\" data-content=\"And here's some amazing content. It's very engaging. Right?\">Dismissible popover</a>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"6e3b031e6db2c2025073","html":"\n<span class=\"d-inline-block\" data-toggle=\"popover\" data-content=\"Disabled popover\">\n  <button class=\"btn btn-primary\" style=\"pointer-events: none;\" type=\"button\" disabled=\"\">Disabled button</button>\n</span>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""}],"nav":[{"en":"Getting started","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/introduction/"},{"en":"Introduction","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/introduction/"},{"en":"Download","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/download/"},{"en":"Contents","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/contents/"},{"en":"Browsers & devices","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/browsers-devices/"},{"en":"JavaScript","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/javascript/"},{"en":"Theming","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/theming/"},{"en":"Build tools","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/build-tools/"},{"en":"Webpack","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/webpack/"},{"en":"Accessibility","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/getting-started/accessibility/"},{"en":"Layout","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/layout/overview/"},{"en":"Overview","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/layout/overview/"},{"en":"Grid","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/layout/grid/"},{"en":"Utilities for layout","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.4/layout/utilities-for-layout/"},{"en":"Content","href":"https://getbootstrap.com